        "original_id": "64d8cbf0-0cec-5d7b-8b5f-849d2e80343a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Holdstock, H. L. Mencken\n- Works: Mythago Wood\n- Topics: Fantasy literature, mythic fiction, American English\n\nFacts:\n- H. L. Mencken, born Henry Louis Mencken, lived from September 12, 1880 to January 29, 1956 and was an American journalist, satirist, cultural critic, and scholar of American English.\n- Robert Holdstock, born Robert Paul Holdstock, lived from 2 August 1948 to 29 November 2009 and was an English novelist and author.\n- Robert Holdstock was best known for Celtic, Nordic, Gothic, and Pictish fantasy literature, mainly in the fantasy subgenre of mythic fiction.\n- Mythago Wood is a fantasy novel by British writer Robert Holdstock that was published in the United Kingdom in 1984.",
